Z||000036||loafer87gt||08-05-2001||03:39 PM||||The ending kinda threw me for a loop as well. My theory is that after Marky M. went missing, his crew back on the main ship sent out several more probes guided by chimps to look for him. Maybe one of these highly trained chimps got send back to prehistoric earth and were more advanced than the humans at the time, becoming the dominant species. I also found this snippet on a movie site:<P>quote:<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>HOLLYWOOD (Zap2it.com) - Much of the anticipation for the "Planet of the Apes" remake has surrounded the ending. How in the hell were they going top the original's Statue of Liberty scene, one of the most indelible finales ever?<BR>Now that the picture has opened, the new coda director Tim Burton and company have concocted has confounded critics and audiences alike. No matter how many times they go over it, every theory they come up with either stretches plausibility to the point of snapping or contradicts the movie's own internal logic in some way.<P>In an exclusive interview on Sunday, Zap2it.com asks 20th Century Fox's head of distribution Bruce Snyder to explain it, to uncover the missing link, if you will.<P>WARNING: If you don't want to have even a hint of the ending revealed, do not read further.<P>High off of the picture's record-breaking $68.5 million opening, Snyder laughs heartily at the question. "Actually, you're not supposed to be able to (explain it)," he reveals. "If the truth be known, it wasn't really supposed to make sense. It was just supposed to go 'whoa,' make you think. Now is he in another world, did he go back in time, did he get forward in time?"<P>"The reality is there's no firm answer to that," he advises. "It's whatever you want it to be."<P>"Everybody keeps looking for (the answer), but you've got to remember you just watched a movie about talking monkeys in outer space," he explains. "Don't look for too much logic, you know." He laughs again.<P>Maybe the inevitable sequel will clear things up, but Snyder says that one hasn't been given the go ahead just yet. "But I hope somebody's writing it as we speak," he offers. "This looks like a franchise," adding that Burton and the cast are "ecstatic."<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000037||DecadenceR||08-05-2001||08:48 PM||||Well now we know that it means whatever we want it to. LOL<BR>YOu gotta love these movies though, cause they always talk perfect english in the new world that the guy finds or crashes in and stuff like that. Universal communication. You can go to another planet and know exactly what they're saying, but you can't go to aother country on the same planet and know what they're saying.....||||reg||1
Z||000038||My7Fieros||08-06-2001||12:08 AM||||Well I just got home from seeing it...LOVED IT!!! Yeah, the ending was kinda "huh"? But I read all the responses to this post (didnt before, didnt want to know what happened at the end) and kinda came to the same conclusion. But, like that article says, format whatever opinion of what you think happened....it obviously wansnt supposed to make a whole lotta sense. <BR>I really dug the movie though...prob go see it again!<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||14
